# Project Template

Use this template when creating new projects in `projects/`.

## Structure

```
projects/<project-name>/
├── .opencode/              # Project-specific OpenCode config
│   ├── agents/             # Custom agents
│   ├── commands/           # Custom commands
│   └── settings.jsonc      # Project settings override
├── src/                    # Source code
├── tests/                  # Tests
├── docs/                   # Documentation
├── scripts/                # Build/deploy scripts
├── .gitignore
├── README.md
├── AGENTS.md               # Project-specific agent instructions
├── package.json / pyproject.toml / Cargo.toml / go.mod
└── CLAUDE.md               # For Claude Code compatibility
```

## Quick Start

```bash
# Copy template
cp -r templates/project-template projects/my-project

# Or use the script
./scripts/new-project.sh my-project
```

## Required Files

Every project should have:

1. **README.md** - Project overview, setup, usage
2. **AGENTS.md** - Project-specific instructions for agents
3. **.gitignore** - Appropriate for the language
4. **License** - If open source

## Language-Specific Templates

- `templates/python-project/` - Python with uv, pytest, ruff
- `templates/node-project/` - Node/TypeScript with vitest, eslint
- `templates/rust-project/` - Rust with cargo
- `templates/go-project/` - Go with modules

## OpenCode Project Config

Create `.opencode/settings.jsonc`:

```jsonc
{
  "model": { "provider": "kilo", "model": "kilo/kilo-auto/free" },
  "agents": {
    "default": "project-main",
    "project-main": {
      "systemPrompt": "You are working on <project-name>. Follow AGENTS.md.",
      "permissions": { "tools": ["*"] }
    }
  },
  "skills": { "directories": ["${workspace}/.opencode/skills"] }
}
```